mail — read mail over IMAP into the shared store and search it, with app passwords kept in the OS
keyring

Usage: mail <profile> <command> [options]
Account commands start with your profile, a name you choose; none is ever assumed.

Works with:
  tg                      Telegram in the same local store: search, review and tasks offline
  max                     MAX in the same local store: search, review and tasks offline
  wa                      WhatsApp in the same local store: search, review and tasks offline
  zm                      Zoom meetings: transcripts and summaries, searchable with your other WireCat data
  drive                   Google Drive and Docs as local text, searchable with your other WireCat data
  gcal                    Google Calendar events, searchable with your other WireCat data
  wcat context <person>   one person across messengers, mail, notes and meetings
  files                   notes folders, Obsidian vaults, PDF and Word files, searchable with your other WireCat data
  b24                     Bitrix24 CRM: deals, leads and pipelines, searchable with your other WireCat data
  amo                     amoCRM and Kommo: deals, contacts and companies, searchable with your other WireCat data
  attio                   Attio CRM: deals, people and companies, searchable with your other WireCat data
  pbx                     Asterisk PBX calls and recordings, searchable with your other WireCat data
  notion                  Notion pages and databases as local text, searchable with your other WireCat data
  ydisk                   Yandex Disk folders as local text, searchable with your other WireCat data
  wordpress               WordPress posts and pages, searchable with your other WireCat data
  linear                  Linear issues and projects, searchable with your other WireCat data

Start here:   mail personal session start --address <email>  (any profile name works)
              mail session list                              your profiles and their logged-in accounts
Next:         mail commands                                  every command, by section
              mail help options                              output, offline, timeouts, dry run
For agents:   mail skill show                                rules and the discovery loop
